  "paths": {
    "docs/concepts/work-loop.md": "Explicit result and optional promise; thirteen states, terminal field, report versus landing completion, inherited destinations/holds, current stale-claim attention, artifact audit, canonical citation admission, dated world staleness.",
    "docs/reference/gs/status.md": "Preserves durable versus advisory status distinctions; replaces obsolete Work counts with actual Table/Graph populations and proposal count, and corrects dated world-staleness and succession explanations.",
    "docs/reference/gs/work.md": "Five default relationship lanes plus explicit audit lane, optional false-versus-absent debt filter, closed debt exception and current Git observations outside the durable cursor.",
    "docs/reference/mcp/status.md": "Direct reporting-artifact next act, hold owner, closed transfer without a terminal value, bounded status omission versus work audit selection.",
    "docs/reference/mcp/work.md": "Exact query choices and omission policy; fold-selected approval/candidate versus latest review; receipt/terminal and approved-artifact carry transfer.",
    "docs/reference/architecture.md": "Reconciles layers 2, 5, 6 and 7 with delivered request/hold/status/query/UI behavior; removes future-policy contradictions and distinguishes actual claimed-stale attention from the separately commissioned recovery. No architecture contract changes.",
    "docs/reference/gs/merge.md": "State@3 held/unheld versus legacy authorization, exact destination/release signer and act-time checks, compatibility receipt warning, dated world staleness, unchanged carried/sibling/abandoned exact-path rules and reader-deployment boundary.",
    "SKILL.md": "Keeps adopted discipline; aligns next actor and query triage with delivered behavior, retains instruction to honor holds despite the tool compatibility window, and corrects citation admission and exact cited-revision preview guidance."
  },
